    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0768" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg678"/>

                <head>No. 304.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29, 1875</date>.
                        (Received May 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 324.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Carter, Hawaiian commissioner to
                    Washington, returned on the 8th instant, bringing the treaty of reciprocity
                    between the United States and this kingdom, as ratified by the United States
                    Senate.</p>
                <pb facs="0769" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/>
                <p>The King and his government and the Hawaiian people, and foreigners generally,
                    received the news with intense delight.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>It is reported that the King has also ratified the treaty, and that it will be
                    transmitted to Washington, by special messenger, in course a few days.</p>
                <p>With great respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY A. PEIRCE</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
